    "privacy": {
      "back": "← Back to Godesia",
      "changes": "<p>If this policy changes, the date in the header will be updated and, where the change is significant, account holders will be notified by email.</p>",
      "controller": "<p><strong>Enric Godes</strong> — contact: <a href=\"mailto:egodes@vasava.es\">egodes@vasava.es</a>.</p><p>Purpose: to preserve and share the Godes family genealogical archive within a closed family circle.</p>",
      "cookies": "<p>A <strong>single technical cookie</strong> is used, <code>godesia_session</code>, which keeps you signed in for 30 days. It is essential in order to log in and, being strictly necessary, it requires no prior consent. There are no analytics or advertising cookies, and no third-party cookies.</p>",
      "data": "<ul><li><strong>Genealogical data:</strong> names, dates and places of birth, baptism, marriage and death, occupations, residences, burials, photographs, documents and family notes. Most of it concerns <strong>deceased people</strong> (about 1,300 of the 1,489 records).</li><li><strong>Living people:</strong> around 170 records, with data supplied by the family itself.</li><li><strong>User accounts:</strong> name, email address, hashed password and date of last access.</li><li><strong>Contributions:</strong> whatever you send through the collaboration form (name, email, message and attachments).</li><li><strong>Technical log:</strong> questions the search engine could not answer, kept in order to improve it.</li></ul>",
      "deceased": "<p>The GDPR does not apply to data about deceased people, who make up most of this archive. Even so, their heirs or relatives may ask for any record to be corrected or removed, and such a request is honoured exactly as if the regulation applied (Art. 3 of the Spanish LOPDGDD).</p>",
      "h_changes": "Changes",
      "h_controller": "Controller",
      "h_cookies": "Cookies",
      "h_data": "What data is held",
      "h_deceased": "Deceased people",
      "h_hosting": "Where the data is hosted",
      "h_purpose": "Purpose and legal basis",
      "h_retention": "Retention",
      "h_rights": "Your rights",
      "h_security": "Security",
      "h_third": "Third parties involved",
      "hosting": "<p>The application, the database and the photographs are hosted on <strong>Railway</strong> (Railway Corporation, USA), in its <strong>us-east4 region, Virginia (United States)</strong>.</p><p>This involves an <strong>international transfer of data</strong> outside the European Economic Area, covered by the European Commission's standard contractual clauses included in Railway's data processing agreement.</p><p>The controller also keeps backups on personal equipment in Spain. No other copy or hosting exists.</p>",
      "intro": "<p>Godesia is a <strong>private</strong> family genealogical archive: non-commercial, ad-free and closed to search engines. Only people who are individually approved can get in. This page explains what data is held, where it is hosted and what you can ask for regarding your own.</p>",
      "purpose": "<p>The data is used <strong>solely</strong> to maintain the genealogical archive and give the family access to it.</p><ul><li>Genealogical data: legitimate interest in historical and family research (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li><li>User accounts: managing the access the person requested themselves (Art. 6(1)(a) and 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li></ul><p>There is no automated decision-making and no profiling. <strong>No data is sold, transferred or shared with third parties</strong> for commercial purposes, and there is no advertising of any kind.</p>",
      "retention": "<ul><li>Genealogical data is kept indefinitely: preserving it is precisely the purpose of the archive.</li><li>Accounts are kept while they remain active; if you ask to be removed, the account and its sessions are deleted.</li><li>Sessions expire after 30 days; password-recovery links after 2 hours.</li></ul>",
      "rights": "<p>You may exercise your rights of <strong>access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability</strong> at any time.</p><p>Just write to <a href=\"mailto:egodes@vasava.es\">egodes@vasava.es</a> or use the collaboration form on this site. You will get an answer within one month at most. If you ask for your own record, or that of a living relative, to be removed, <strong>it is done without asking for reasons</strong>.</p><p>If you believe your data has not been handled properly, you may lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data Protection Agency (<a href=\"https://www.aepd.es\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.aepd.es</a>).</p>",
      "security": "<ul><li>The whole site requires an active session: pages, photographs, documents and queries. Nothing is accessible without an approved account.</li><li>Registrations are approved <strong>manually, one by one</strong>. Access can be revoked at any time and the session ends immediately.</li><li>Passwords are stored with <strong>PBKDF2-SHA256 and 200,000 iterations with a random salt</strong>: never in plain text. Nobody, not even the controller, can read them.</li><li>Accounts live in a database that is <strong>separate</strong> from the genealogical one.</li><li>All traffic is encrypted with HTTPS.</li></ul>",
      "third": "<ul><li><strong>Railway</strong> — server and data hosting.</li><li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivery of access and password-recovery emails; it receives the recipient's email address.</li><li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>, the stylesheet CDN and the <strong>Esri</strong> and <strong>OpenStreetMap</strong> map tiles — when the page loads they see the visitor's IP address, as on any website using these services. They receive no family-tree data.</li></ul><p>There is no Google Analytics or any other analytics tool, no trackers, no advertising pixels and no social network buttons.</p>",
      "title": "Privacy and data protection",
      "updated": "Last updated: 22 September 2026"
    },
